{"seq":42,"ts":"2026-08-24T10:55:38.992Z","type":"work.add","payload":{"id":"tsk-198","title":"Bug: mergeRunnerItemLocked's isUnchangedSinceBranchHeadAtTake (tsk-4s6, src/runner/merge.mjs, next…","description":"Bug: mergeRunnerItemLocked's isUnchangedSinceBranchHeadAtTake (tsk-4s6, src/runner/merge.mjs, next to isMergeUnionPath) uses blob-equality (git rev-parse <branchHeadAtTake>:<path> vs <branch>:<path>) to prove a .fgos/ path is safe to restore to main's HEAD -- but blob-equality throws (caught, returns false) when the path never existed on the branch at branchHeadAtTake at all, so a path the branch never possessed at any point (not merely 'unchanged since fork') still falls through to fgos-write-rejected even though the branch contributed literally nothing to it. Confirmed live merging fgw/tsk-25b (tsk-4s6's own fix already resolved 2 of its original 3 blocked paths -- config.json, legacy events.jsonl -- both genuinely unchanged since branchHeadAtTake): the one remaining path is .fgos/events.jsonl.backup-tsk-1lv-4-dedup-fix-20260817, present at the merge-base and on main's current HEAD, absent both from the branch's branchHeadAtTake commit AND its current tip (git rev-parse branchHeadAtTake:<path> throws 'exists on disk, but not in <ref>') -- the branch never introduced this path at all. Fix: widen isUnchangedSinceBranchHeadAtTake's proof from blob-equality to a real no-diff check (e.g. execFileSync git diff --quiet <branchHeadAtTake> <branch> -- <path>, exit 0 means no diff) -- this naturally covers both 'blob identical on both sides' (today's case) and 'path absent on both sides' (this gap), with zero new risk since 'no diff at all' is a strictly weaker, safer claim than blob-equality was already making. Mirror tsk-4s6's own test pattern (test/runner/merge.test.mjs) with a case where the .fgos/ path is absent at branchHeadAtTake, absent on the branch's current tip, and present+drifted on main.","kind":"bug","status":"todo","deps":[],"risk":"standard","refs":[